Package: argusrm-server
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: avahi-daemon
Description: Argus Remote Manager server
 Argus Remote Manager enrolls managed machines, provides authenticated
 downloads, and coordinates remote management operations.

Package: argusrm-agent-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: avahi-daemon
Replaces: argusrm-agent (<< 0.1.1-1)
Breaks: argusrm-agent (<< 0.1.1-1)
Description: Argus Remote Manager command-line agent
 This package installs the agent on a managed Linux machine. The command
 is argus-agent-cli. It does not use GTK. Registration from the command
 line enables and starts its systemd or SysV service. This is the package
 to install on a server.

Package: argusrm-agent-gtk
Architecture: any
Depends: argusrm-agent-cli (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: avahi-daemon
Replaces: argusrm-agent (<< 0.1.1-1)
Breaks: argusrm-agent (<< 0.1.1-1)
Description: Argus Remote Manager agent with a registration window
 This package adds the argus-agent command, which opens a desktop window
 for registration. The service itself is the command-line agent. Install
 argusrm-agent-cli alone on a machine without a desktop.

Package: argusrm-controller
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Argus Remote Manager controller
 This package contains the desktop and command-line controller. It enrolls
 with an Argus Remote Manager server, lists agents, and runs a command on
 one agent.
